  "summary": "Both previous analyses correctly identify the root cause: getKey() is defined inside {{if .ShowKeyModal}} blocks and becomes undefined when users are already authenticated. However, the second proposal's recommendation to 'just move getKey() out of the ShowKeyModal conditional' overlooks a subtlety in client.html: there is no {{end}} for ShowKeyModal before a separate {{if .Authenticated}} block — instead, the ShowKeyModal block at line 286 ends at line 346 with {{end}}, and the main script block starting at line 495 is unconditional. This means client.html's edit functions (lines 1117/1158/1196/1254) are already in an unconditional scope and the fix there is simply to replace getKey() calls with _dashKey (line 497), which is always available and already used by restartClient (line 634) and all other API calls. For index.html, the edit functions (lines 763/804/842/900) are inside the {{if .Authenticated}} block where the IIFE-defined 'key' variable (line 386) is already in scope — so the fix is to remove 'var key = getKey()' and just use the existing 'key' variable directly. The logout() issue in client.html (defined at line 331 inside ShowKeyModal, called at line 349) should also be fixed by moving it outside the conditional. The cleanest approach is file-specific: in client.html, replace getKey() calls with _dashKey and move logout() out; in index.html, remove the redundant 'var key = getKey()' lines in edit functions (since 'key' is already a closure variable), and move restartClient() out of ShowKeyModal."
